    {
      "type": "card",
      "algo": 5,
      "deck": "Leetcode program med free 2",
      "question": "<a href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/partition-list\" target=\"_blank\">86. Partition List</a>",
      "number": 2,
      "hint": null,
      "notes": "",
      "explanation": "Create two separate linked lists: one for nodes less than x and one for nodes greater than or equal to x. Iterate through the original list, appending nodes to the appropriate new list. Finally, connect the tail of the 'less than' list to the head of the 'greater or equal' list.\nTime complexity: O(n), Space complexity: O(1) (if modifying pointers in place, not O(n) for new lists if nodes are reused)\nAlgorithms: Linked List Manipulation, Two Pointers (for managing new lists)\nData Structures: Linked List\nKey concepts: List partitioning, Pointer management, Maintaining relative order",
