    {
      "type": "card",
      "algo": 5,
      "deck": "Leetcode program med free 2",
      "question": "<a href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/subsets-ii\" target=\"_blank\">90. Subsets II</a>",
      "number": 4,
      "hint": null,
      "notes": "",
      "explanation": "Use a backtracking approach. Sort the input array to handle duplicates easily. In the recursive step, if the current number is the same as the previous and the previous was not included in the path (by skipping it in the for loop iteration), skip the current number to avoid duplicate subsets.\nTime complexity: O(N * 2^N), Space complexity: O(N) for recursion stack and current subset\nAlgorithms: Backtracking, Recursion, Sorting\nData Structures: Array, List\nKey concepts: Power set with duplicates, Duplicate handling in subsets, Depth-first search",
