    {
      "type": "card",
      "algo": 5,
      "deck": "Leetcode program med free 2",
      "question": "<a href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/decode-ways\" target=\"_blank\">91. Decode Ways</a>",
      "number": 5,
      "hint": null,
      "notes": "",
      "explanation": "Use dynamic programming. dp[i] will be the number of ways to decode the substring s[0...i-1]. If s[i-1] is not '0', dp[i] += dp[i-1]. If s[i-2]s[i-1] forms a valid two-digit code (10-26), dp[i] += dp[i-2]. Handle edge cases like leading zeros.\nTime complexity: O(n), Space complexity: O(n) or O(1) with space optimization\nAlgorithms: Dynamic Programming\nData Structures: Array (for DP table), String\nKey concepts: String decoding, DP state definition, Overlapping subproblems",
