      "question": "<a href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/restore-ip-addresses\" target=\"_blank\">93. Restore IP Addresses</a>",
      "number": 7,
      "hint": null,
      "notes": "",
      "explanation": "Use a backtracking approach. Try to form 4 valid segments (0-255, no leading zeros unless the number is 0 itself) from the input string. At each step, try to form the next segment of length 1, 2, or 3 characters, ensuring it's a valid IP segment.\nTime complexity: Roughly O(1) because the number of segments is fixed at 4 and length of string is small (max 12 for valid IPs). More precisely, constant factor related to 3^4. Space complexity: O(1) for storing results (max string length is fixed).\nAlgorithms: Backtracking, Recursion, String Parsing\nData Structures: String, List\nKey concepts: IP address validation rules, Segment generation, Depth-first search",
