    {
      "type": "card",
      "algo": 5,
      "deck": "Leetcode program med free 2",
      "question": "<a href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/unique-binary-search-trees\" target=\"_blank\">96. Unique Binary Search Trees</a>",
      "number": 9,
      "hint": null,
      "notes": "",
      "explanation": "This is a Catalan number problem. Use dynamic programming. dp[i] represents the number of unique BSTs that can be formed with i nodes. dp[i] = sum(dp[j-1] * dp[i-j]) for j from 1 to i (j is the root, j-1 nodes in left subtree, i-j nodes in right). dp[0] = 1.\nTime complexity: O(n^2), Space complexity: O(n)\nAlgorithms: Dynamic Programming\nData Structures: Array (for DP table)\nKey concepts: Catalan numbers, BST structure, DP recurrence relation",
      "answers": [
        {
          "id": 133012,
          "text": "Reservoir sampling algorithm",
          "number": 1,
