      "question": "<a href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/recover-binary-search-tree\" target=\"_blank\">99. Recover Binary Search Tree</a>",
      "number": 12,
      "hint": null,
      "notes": "",
      "explanation": "Perform an in-order traversal. Find the two nodes that are swapped by identifying the violations of the sorted order (first_node where prev.val &gt; curr.val, and second_node where prev.val &gt; curr.val again or the last curr in first violation). Then swap their values. For O(1) space, use Morris Traversal.\nTime complexity: O(n) for in-order traversal, Space complexity: O(h) for recursion or O(1) with Morris Traversal\nAlgorithms: In-order Traversal, Morris Traversal (for O(1) space)\nData Structures: Binary Tree\nKey concepts: BST properties, Identifying swapped nodes, In-place recovery",
