      "question": "<a href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/flatten-binary-tree-to-linked-list\" target=\"_blank\">114. Flatten Binary Tree to Linked List</a>",
      "number": 20,
      "hint": null,
      "notes": "",
      "explanation": "Perform a modified pre-order traversal (right, left, root). Keep track of the previously processed node ('prev'). For each current node, set its right child to 'prev', its left child to null, and then update 'prev' to be the current node. Or, recursively flatten left and right subtrees, then connect root -&gt; flattened_left -&gt; flattened_right.\nTime complexity: O(n), Space complexity: O(h) for recursion or O(1) with Morris-like traversal modification.\nAlgorithms: Depth-First Search (DFS), Tree Traversal (modified pre-order or post-order)\nData Structures: Binary Tree\nKey concepts: In-place modification, Tree to list conversion, Pointer rewiring",
