    {
      "type": "card",
      "algo": 5,
      "deck": "Leetcode program med free 2",
      "question": "<a href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/populating-next-right-pointers-in-each-node\" target=\"_blank\">116. Populating Next Right Pointers in Each Node</a>",
      "number": 21,
      "hint": null,
      "notes": "",
      "explanation": "Use BFS. For each node dequeued, its 'next' pointer is the next node in the queue (if it's not the last on its level). Or, use DFS: for a node, if its left child exists, left.next = right. If node.next exists and node.right exists, right.next = node.next.left. Perfect binary tree property helps.\nTime complexity: O(n), Space complexity: O(w) for BFS queue or O(h) for DFS recursion (for perfect tree, h = log n, w = n/2). O(1) space solution exists using level iteration.\nAlgorithms: Breadth-First Search (BFS), Depth-First Search (DFS), Level Iteration\nData Structures: Perfect Binary Tree (with 'next' pointer)\nKey concepts: Level linking, Next pointer population, Tree traversal variants",
      "answers": [
        {
          "id": 133024,
          "text": "Bit manipulation with XOR",
          "number": 1,
          "isCorrect": 1,
          "groupIndex": 1
