      "explanation": "Use two stacks: one for the actual values and another to store the minimum element found so far at each point. When pushing, if the new element is &lt;= current min, push to min_stack. When popping, if popped element == top of min_stack, pop from min_stack too. Or, store pairs (value, current_min) in a single stack.\nTime complexity: O(1) for all operations. Space complexity: O(n) in worst case.\nAlgorithms: Stack operations\nData Structures: Stack\nKey concepts: Auxiliary data structure for tracking minimum, Synchronized stack operations",
