      "question": "<a href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/find-peak-element\" target=\"_blank\">162. Find Peak Element</a>",
      "number": 44,
      "hint": null,
      "notes": "",
      "explanation": "Use a modified binary search. If nums[mid] &lt; nums[mid+1], a peak must be in the right half (mid+1 to high). If nums[mid] &gt; nums[mid+1] (or mid is last element), a peak could be nums[mid] or in the left half. The condition nums[i] != nums[i+1] simplifies comparisons. The problem guarantees a peak exists.\nTime complexity: O(log n), Space complexity: O(1)\nAlgorithms: Binary Search (modified)\nData Structures: Array\nKey concepts: Peak definition, Property of adjacent elements, Search space reduction based on slope",
