      "question": "<a href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/maximum-gap\" target=\"_blank\">164. Maximum Gap</a>",
      "number": 45,
      "hint": null,
      "notes": "",
      "explanation": "Use bucket sort or radix sort ideas. Find min and max values. Create buckets of size (max-min)/(n-1). Distribute numbers into buckets, storing only min/max per bucket. The max gap must be between max of one bucket and min of the next non-empty bucket. If n &lt; 2, return 0.\nTime complexity: O(n) for bucket sort if range is manageable or radix sort. O(n log n) if standard sort is used first. Space complexity: O(n) for buckets or O(1) if sorting in place and then iterating.\nAlgorithms: Bucket Sort (Pigeonhole Principle), Radix Sort\nData Structures: Array, Buckets (can be arrays or lists)\nKey concepts: Non-comparison sort, Gap calculation between buckets, Range partitioning",
