      "number": 50,
      "hint": null,
      "notes": "",
      "explanation": "Implement controlled in-order traversal. Use a stack. In the constructor or first `next()` call, push all left children of the root onto the stack. `next()` pops from stack (this is the smallest), then pushes all left children of its right child. `hasNext()` checks if stack is not empty.\\\\nTime complexity: O(1) average for next() and hasNext() (amortized over N calls is O(N)). Space complexity: O(h) for the stack.\\\\nAlgorithms: In-order Traversal (Iterative), Stack\\\\nData Structures: Binary Search Tree, Stack\\\\nKey concepts: Iterator design, Flattening BST implicitly, Controlled traversal",
